<title>FRANCE: Socialists plan public audit within two weeks.</title>
<headline>Socialists plan public audit within two weeks.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Socialists are likely to carry out a promised audit of public finances during their first two weeks in office, party spokesman Francois Hollande said on Monday.</p>
<p>Socialist leader Lionel Jospin said during the campaign that the audit of public finances would be his party's first act if elected, to see if they were as robust as Prime Minister Alain Juppe's outgoing government had said.</p>
<p>Hollande told France Inter radio on Monday the examination was likely to be carried out &quot;during the coming two weeks&quot;.</p>
</text>
